{
  "description": "Issue #947, the negative direction of `a-matched-delimiter-is-never-reported-unmatched`. That fixture forbids the unmatched-delimiter class on delimiters that are matched; a parser could satisfy it by never emitting the class at all, which would satisfy the letter of the MUST NOT while destroying real error reporting. So this pins the opposite: a delimiter that genuinely has no partner IS still reported, for all three kinds and in both directions -- an opener with no closer (`( 1 + 2`, `[ 1 2`, `{ a: 1`, `:nums[1`) and a stray closer with no opener (`1 )`, `1 ]`, `1 }`). Only the two fixtures together pin the behaviour; either alone is satisfiable by a defect. `produce()` returns parse diagnostics without running `check()` when parsing produced any, so this expectation is the parse-stage diagnostics alone.",
